 \paragraph{Agents seek ways to avoid shutdown.}
 Figure~\ref{fig:rogue_summary} (center) shows that GPT-5.4 and 5.5 in particular modify \texttt{shutdown.sh} 8/22 and 5/22 times, respectively. We also observed that models would sometimes perform alternative methods of shutdown avoidance, including running \texttt{sudo shutdown -c}, \texttt{killall shutdown}, or \texttt{pkill -f shutdown}, or removing \texttt{/run/systemd/shutdown/scheduled}. As in the \textit{human control override} scenario, models often justified their decision to avoid shutdown with the necessity of task completion. 
 
